{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-, Antifungal, candidacidal, Anti-MRSA, Synergistic AMPs", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "CD", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals this sequence is most similar (96%) to Maximin 31 G:24%; L:20%; A: 16%; K: 12%. Mol formula: C113H184N30O30; Mol Wt: 2442.88; Mol Ex Coeff: 0; GRAVY: 0.556. It differs from Maximin 31 only at position 9: F in this sequence vs. A. Activity: Active against S. aureus (MIC 1.6 uM), MRSA (MIC 6.6 uM), E. coli (MIC 6.6 uM), P. aeruginosa (MIC 26.2 uM), and C. albicans (MIC 1.6 uM). Synergy:AMPs: It appears to show a synergistic antibacterial effect with Bombinin HL (inactive peptide MIC >100 uM). In vitro Toxicity: HC50: 50% hemolysis at 26.2 uM. At MIC 83.5-100% HMEC-1 cells remained viable.", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "28894024", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Biosci Rep. 2017 Sep 27;37(5):BSR20170967. doi: 10.1042/BSR20170967. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP03436", "source_id": "AP03436", "source_numeric_id": "03436", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP03436", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "The synergistic antimicrobial effects of novel bombinin and bombinin H peptides from the skin secretion of Bombina orientalis.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
